q('ai-excel','medium','A generated spreadsheet formula works on one example. What should you do before using it across the model?', ['Test boundaries, missing values, references, and expected outputs','Assume one result proves all cases','Paste it into every sheet without review','Replace the source data to fit the formula'],0,'One example cannot establish correctness across ranges, edge cases, or changing assumptions.'),
q('ai-presentations','medium','An AI-created slide contains a market-size estimate with no source. What is the best treatment?', ['Verify and source the estimate or remove it','Label it audited','Use the precise number to imply confidence','Cite the slide itself as evidence'],0,'The underlying evidence must support the claim; the generated slide is not an independent source.'),
m('ai-model-checking','hard','AI reports no problems in a model, but cash does not reconcile. Select all justified actions.', ['Investigate the reconciliation directly','Check the scope and inputs the tool actually reviewed','Treat the AI result as conclusive assurance','Document and resolve the broken linkage before use'],[0,1,3],'AI review is assistance, not assurance. A failed financial check requires direct investigation regardless of a generated verdict.'),
q('ai-company-research','hard','Two AI summaries agree on a company figure, but both derive from the same unsourced article. What is missing?', ['Independent verification against an authoritative source','A third paraphrase of the same article','A more confident writing style','A larger font'],0,'Agreement between derivative outputs is not independent corroboration. Trace the figure to an authoritative source.'),
m('ai-confidentiality','hard','A teammate suggests anonymizing a live deal before using an unapproved tool. Select all correct concerns.', ['Distinctive facts may still identify the client','Removing a name does not establish permission','Tool approval and data policy still apply','Anonymization always guarantees safety'],[0,1,2],'Redaction can reduce exposure but does not automatically remove identifiability or satisfy tool and data-handling requirements.')
